// A dev-tier block `@test { … }` (object-model slice 6) is co-located developer-tooling content
// that the build includes only when its tier is **active**. With no tier active (a normal run / the
// conformance harness), the block is **stripped before lowering** — its `fn`s are never compiled or
// run, so its side effects are absent and the program's own output is unchanged. The strip happens
// identically on both backends (both lower the same program), so the differential agrees.
// expect: stdout "5"
// expect: stdout "done"
// expect: exit 0
fn add(a: int, b: int): int { return a + b; }

@test {
    fn adds() { echo "the test body must not run"; }
    fn also() { echo "neither must this"; }
}

echo add(2, 3);
echo "done";
